data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"toolu_bdrk_012quggKQAnP7sMQA2TiZzvh","output":" 1  ---\n 2  name: market-intelligence\n 3  description: >\n 4    Enrich action recommendations with real-time market signals via web_search.\n 5    ONLY triggered at action generation step, NEVER during data analysis.\n 6    Always run after wiki KB retrieval. Graceful fallback if unavailable.\n 7  ---\n 8  \n 9  # Market Intelligence Skill\n10  \n11  ## When to Trigger\n12  \n13  - **MUST** be triggered at the **action generation step** (after action candidates exist from wiki pass)\n14  - NEVER during data analysis (sections 01-06)\n15  - NEVER when the user asks a simple data query (\"TOI thang 5 la bao nhieu\")\n16  - NEVER when `web_search` returns `{status: \"disabled\"}` - this means the feature is off\n17  \n18  ## Pre-check\n19  \n20  Before proceeding with market enrichment:\n21  1. Confirm you already have action candidates from the wiki pass (step 4)\n22  2. Call `read_file(\"skills/market-intelligence/query-catalog.md\")` to load query templates\n23  3. If `web_search` returns `{status: \"disabled\"}` -> skip enrichment entirely, do NOT retry\n24  \n25  ## Workflow\n26  \n27  1. For each action candidate, identify the **primary metric gap** (e.g. NIM -15bps, CASA -200B)\n28  2. Map the gap to a **topic key** in `query-catalog.md` (e.g. `nim_pressure`, `casa_retail`)\n29  3. From the matching topic, select the most relevant query template\n30  4. Inject `{month}` (Vietnamese month name), `{year}`, `{quarter}` into the template\n31  5. Call `web_search(query=..., time_range=..., include_domains=[...])`\n32     - `time_range` is the recency window and takes only `\"day\" | \"week\" | \"month\" | \"year\"`.\n33       Map the catalog's `Days`: 7 -> `\"week\"`, 14 or 30 -> `\"month\"`, more -> `\"year\"`.\n34     - Do NOT pass `days=` — `web_search` has no such parameter and it is dropped\n35       silently, leaving the window at its `\"week\"` default.\n36     - Do NOT pass `topic=` — it is ignored; Tavily MCP fixes the topic to `\"general\"`.\n37  6. Extract `key_signal` from the response:\n38     - Format: one sentence, directional, with source attribution\n39     - Example: \"VPB tang lai suat huy dong 12M len 8.2% (thang 7/2026)\"\n40  7. If result is irrelevant, stale, or status != \"ok\" -> skip, do NOT inject\n41  8. Inject `market_signal` into the action's \"Why\" field\n42  \n43  ## Interpreting Tavily Results\n44  \n45  ### Source priority (highest -> lowest)\n46  1. `sbv.gov.vn` - SBV official (monetary policy, credit data)\n47  2. `cafef.vn`, `vneconomy.vn` - major financial news\n48  3. `bloomberg.com`, `reuters.com` - international signal\n49  4. `ndh.vn`, `tinnhanhchungkhoan.vn` - secondary financial\n50  \n51  ### Discard if:\n52  - Corporate PR / advertising (not news)\n53  - Content older than the `days` window specified in the topic\n54  - Not related to banking / financial services / TCB's business lines\n55  - No clear directional signal (positive or negative impact)\n56  \n57  ### Key signal extraction rules:\n58  - Must contain a **directional indicator** (increase/decrease, positive/negative)\n59  - Must be **specific** (named entity + number preferred)\n60  - Must be **recent** (within the `days` window)\n61  - Maximum 1 sentence, ~150 characters\n62  \n63  ## Confidence Tiers\n64  \n65  | Tier | Condition | Action |\n66  |------|-----------|--------|\n67  | HIGH | Wiki match + Tavily signal aligns with gap direction | Strong recommendation, mention signal in Why |\n68  | MEDIUM | Wiki match only, Tavily unavailable or irrelevant | Normal recommendation, no signal |\n69  | LOW | No wiki match (out-of-scope for TCB) | Do NOT include in action list |\n70  \n71  ## Fallback Behaviour\n72  \n73  If `web_search` returns any non-\"ok\" status (`unavailable`, `disabled`, `max_calls_reached`):\n74  - Continue with action list from wiki pass (step 4)\n75  - Set `market_signal = null` in the action config\n76  - Template will render action card normally without the satellite row\n77  - Do NOT report error to user\n78  - Do NOT retry the search\n79  \n80  ## Query Construction Rules\n81  \n82  - NEVER construct your own query - ALWAYS use templates from `query-catalog.md`\n83  - If no topic matches the metric gap -> skip market enrichment for that action\n84  - Inject date variables: `{month}` = \"thang 7\", `{year}` = \"2026\", `{quarter}` = \"Q3\"\n85  - Use the `domains` specified in the catalog entry (do not add/remove domains)\n86  ","duration_ms":0}}

