data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"toolu_bdrk_01YFtJzDiu913fzCrDRyZ82H","output":" 1  # CIBG Operating Model (CST/MFT/Sector-Led)\n 2  \n 3  ## Metadata\n 4  - Domain: cibg\n 5  - Category: organization\n 6  - Tags: operating-model, CST, MFT, sector-led, performance-management\n 7  - Last updated: 2026-05-07\n 8  - Source: AP26 CIBG Round 2 (EN)_Nov,25 sent.pdf\n 9  \n10  ## Summary\n11  CIBG's 2026 operating model transitions to a sector-led approach with end-to-end responsibility from industry understanding to GTM execution. Key changes: Sectors drive strategy and KPIs, new CST Squads for emerging VVIPs, MFT restructured to Model 3 (Transaction Banking MFT + Lending MFT) with unified KRAs.\n12  \n13  ## Detail\n14  \n15  ### Model Overview\n16  \n17  The CIBG operating model has three interconnected components:\n18  1. **Sector-led Strategy**: End-to-end from industry expertise to GTM\n19  2. **CST (Client Solution Team)**: Dedicated teams for VVIP segments\n20  3. **MFT (Multi-Functional Team)**: Cross-functional Biz-Tech-Ops execution teams\n21  \n22  ### Sector-Led Model\n23  \n24  #### Scope of Work\n25  \n26  | Function | Responsibility |\n27  |----------|---------------|\n28  | Economic Sector | Business planning, CVP expertise, offering requirements, target setting |\n29  | Client Coverage | Managing relationships, developing Account Plans, focal point for internal resources |\n30  | Product Sales | Understanding solutions, constructing/delivering solutions, executing non-lending products |\n31  \n32  #### Execution Flow\n33  \n34  ```\n35  CIBG HOD → Strategic Management → Solution Provider\n36      ↓              ↓                      ↓\n37  Sector-led    Sub-Sectors        Products/Solutions\n38  strategy      (Industry          (Lending, Non-Lending)\n39                expertise)\n40                    ↓\n41                CVP / Offerings → GTM\n42                    ↓\n43                Key Account & Value Chain\n44  ```\n45  \n46  ### Key Changes from Previous Model\n47  \n48  | Component | Before | After (2026) |\n49  |-----------|--------|------|\n50  | Sector role | Focused on industry expertise and CVP/Offerings | E2E: Industries Understanding, CVP, Offerings, GTM, Performance Management |\n51  | CST | 2 CSTs: VVIP1, VVIP5 | Establish new Squads for emerging VVIP domains: Infrastructure, Energy, HSR, Airports |\n52  | MFT | Model 2, 5 MFTs (2 Biz + 3 Tech-build); Separate KRAs | Model 3, 2 MFTs (Transaction Banking + Lending); Unified KRAs for Biz and Tech |\n53  \n54  ### Expected Outcomes\n55  \n56  - Enhanced alignment between planning, CVP design, and execution\n57  - Accelerated execution speed and cross-team synergy\n58  - Investment in capabilities tailored to client needs\n59  - Maintain team stability for efficiency and accountability\n60  - Empower MFT Leaders to guarantee delivery\n61  \n62  ### MFT Structure (2026)\n63  \n64  #### Transaction Banking MFT\n65  - **MFT Lead**: Bui Anh Tuan\n66  - **Total FTE**: 253.3\n67  - **Teams**: 17 squads (T1, P1, P2, L1, C1-C10, M1, M2, S1)\n68  - **Key focus**: Trade Finance, Payment, Collection, Virtual Account, Cash Management\n69  - **Data team**: 10.4 FTE\n70  \n71  #### Lending MFT\n72  - **MFT Lead**: Nguyen Le Ngoc Han\n73  - **Total FTE**: 50.3\n74  - **Chapters**: PO, Segment, Solution, BA, Dev, QE, Agile\n75  - **Sub-teams**: Credit Solution (13.2 FTE), Structured Finance (15.6 FTE), Credit Procedure (18.3 FTE)\n76  \n77  ### Performance Management\n78  \n79  - Unified KRAs assigned and evaluated by the division (not separate Biz vs Tech)\n80  - Sector drives target setting for leading and lagging indicators to CBC and RM\n81  - Performance managed from Industries → Clients → CBC → RM\n82  \n83  ## See Also\n84  - [[cibg-coverage-model]]\n85  - [[cibg-sector-strategy]]\n86  - [[transaction-banking]]\n87  \n88  ## Change History\n89  | Date | Change | Source |\n90  |------|--------|--------|\n91  | 2026-05-07 | Initial creation from AP26 CIBG Round 2 | AP26 CIBG Round 2 (EN)_Nov,25 sent.pdf |\n92  | 2026-05-08 | Moved from cibg/metrics/ to cibg/organization/ — fixed category | Restructure per wiki-schema |","duration_ms":0}}

