data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"toolu_bdrk_012LCdLLUVexpXwCSsUtMmFg","output":"  1  # CIBG Forecast Logic — MMU Segment\n  2  \n  3  ## Metadata\n  4  - Domain: cibg\n  5  - Category: products\n  6  - Tags: forecast, logic-tree, MMU, NII, TOI, balance, active-customer, product-tree\n  7  - Last updated: 2026-05-19\n  8  - Source: D3_Product-Pricing__Product_Tree__CIBG Forecast Logic 2026_MMU segment.md\n  9  \n 10  ## Summary\n 11  Forecast logic tree for CIBG MMU segment (Jan 2025 framework). Defines product-level formulas for projecting NII, TOI, EOP Balance, and Active Customers across all major CIBG product lines: Interbank, Lending, Deposit, LC/Guarantee, Financial Markets, and Payment & Collection.\n 12  \n 13  ## Detail\n 14  \n 15  ### 1. Interbank Products\n 16  **PIC:** Maitt7\n 17  \n 18  | Driver | Formula |\n 19  |--------|---------|\n 20  | EOP Bal → Avg Bal → NII | NII = Avg Bal × Margin (hard margin from FM or market rate for Trade Loan TCB-funded) |\n 21  | Deposit from CIs | NII = Avg Bal × (%CI − %FTP) |\n 22  | Borrowing from CIs | NII = Avg Bal × Margin (Trade Loan margin = 0.2%, Syndication margin = 0.5%) |\n 23  | General | NII = Avg Bal × Margin, where Margin = (%CI − %FTP) |\n 24  \n 25  ### 2. Active Customer Model\n 26  **PIC:** Quynh + Thuy\n 27  \n 28  Active customer forecast uses a churn/reactivation model:\n 29  \n 30  ```\n 31  Active cus = EOP Active cus × (1 − %Churn cus)\n 32             + (%Reactivate × EOP Inactive Y-1)\n 33             + (Total NTB on-board × %Active)\n 34  ```\n 35  \n 36  Model outputs: Active cus count + MOA (Months of Activity).\n 37  \n 38  ### 3. Lending — Product Tree / Customer Tree\n 39  **PIC:** Anhptl2\n 40  \n 41  Decomposition dimensions:\n 42  - **CCY** (currency split)\n 43  - **Fix/Float** (rate type)\n 44  \n 45  | Driver | Formula |\n 46  |--------|---------|\n 47  | Bal movement → EOP Bal → Avg Bal | Linked via net change model |\n 48  | NII | NII = Avg Bal × (%CI + %FTP + %Int revert) |\n 49  | Pipeline | %Contribution (MTD) |\n 50  \n 51  #### EOP Balance Methodology\n 52  \n 53  Base-on net movement of last 3 months:\n 54  - If client has **3 continuous months** increase/decrease → use average of net change over 3 months\n 55  - If client did **NOT** have 3 continuous months increase/decrease → net change = 0 (keep flat)\n 56  \n 57  #### Lending Margin (Normal Lending + VND Loan with rate)\n 58  Margin section ref: 2.1 (Margin), 1 (Balance movement)\n 59  \n 60  ### 4. Deposit — Balance\n 61  **PIC:** taipt4\n 62  \n 63  Balance forecast methodology. ML models applied for CASA/Lending balance prediction.\n 64  \n 65  ### 5. LC Import / Domestic\n 66  **PIC:** linhtp5\n 67  \n 68  | Component | Formula |\n 69  |-----------|---------|\n 70  | NII Existing | Avg Bal × Margin |\n 71  | NII Momentum | Avg Bal × Margin |\n 72  | EOP Balance | EOP Bal Existing + EOP Bal Momentum |\n 73  | Avg Balance | Avg Bal Existing + Avg Bal Momentum |\n 74  | TOI | NII Existing + NII Momentum |\n 75  \n 76  ### 6. Normal Guarantee / SBLC\n 77  **PIC:** linhtp5\n 78  \n 79  | Component | Formula |\n 80  |-----------|---------|\n 81  | NII Existing | TOI Amortized (fee recognized over guarantee life) |\n 82  | NII Momentum | Avg Bal × Margin |\n 83  | EOP Balance | EOP Bal Existing + EOP Bal Momentum |\n 84  | Avg Balance | Avg Bal Existing + Avg Bal Momentum |\n 85  | TOI | NII Existing + NII Momentum |\n 86  \n 87  Note: Guarantee types include automatic/manual frequency — allocation method under review with VVIP team.\n 88  \n 89  ### 7. Financial Market Products\n 90  **PIC:** hadtt3 – hoangvt4\n 91  \n 92  | Product Type | Formula |\n 93  |--------------|---------|\n 94  | NTI (Trading) | NTI = Value × Spread / 1000 |\n 95  | Seasonality adjustment | Avg last 3M × Movement (%MoM LY by subsector_group) |\n 96  | NFI (Carried FWD) | NFI = NFI (Carried FWD) + (New Value × Spread / 1000) |\n 97  | NFI (Margin-based) | NFI = Avg Bal × Margin (1%) |\n 98  \n 99  ### 8. Payment + Collection\n100  **PIC:** maitt7 – hoangvt4\n101  \n102  | Driver | Formula |\n103  |--------|---------|\n104  | Volume | Vol = Active cus × Penetration × Ticket size |\n105  | Value | Val = Active cus × Penetration × Ticket size |\n106  \n107  ## See Also\n108  - [[cibg-product-framework]]\n109  - [[cibg-customer-segmentation]]\n110  - [[rorwa-methodology]]\n111  - [[cost-allocation]]\n112  \n113  ## Change History\n114  | Date | Change | Source |\n115  |------|--------|--------|\n116  | 2026-05-19 | Initial creation — full forecast logic tree for MMU segment | D3_Product-Pricing__Product_Tree__CIBG Forecast Logic 2026_MMU segment.md |","duration_ms":0}}

